  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1210.4 K, melting point of Ge; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 8.830$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.780 + 0.100 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.680 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=8.780\\times10^{-3}T+0.050\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.680\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.850$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1210.4 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 8.156 - 0.973 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.576 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 8.950 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 8.156 + 0.973 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.576 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 4.475 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 28.384 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n1210.4-2000 K: $\\Delta Hr^{\\circ} = -0.144 - 1.992 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 0.110 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 33.850 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = -0.144 + 1.992 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 0.110 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 16.925 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 28.204 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Mills (80). ",
